n invertible function?" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281135 1113 #uuid "8cbc83e7-bc89-5609-b94a-0fe1dfb1bde0" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281135 1145 "A function is invertible if and only if it's a one-to-one function. To determine which of the functions are one-to-one, we use the horizontal line test.\n\nFrom the above, we see that in each of the four given graphs, some horizontal lines intersect the curve more than once. Therefore, these are not one-to-one functions. As a result, none of them correspond to an invertible function." 13194139534184 true] [17592186281136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281137 13194139534184 true] [17592186281136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281138 13194139534184 true] [17592186281136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281139 13194139534184 true] [17592186281136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281140 13194139534184 true] [17592186281136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281141 13194139534184 true] [17592186281136 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534184 true] [17592186281136 1041 "selection" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281136 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281139 13194139534184 true] [17592186281136 1110 #uuid "b8f1bc3a-e66f-59b6-80b4-d09515d80d4c" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281137 1034 "I only" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281137 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534184 true] [17592186281137 1111 #uuid "69069361-8b76-5d0e-a609-f060be54f7e4" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281138 1034 "III only" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281138 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534184 true] [17592186281138 1111 #uuid "796d9c03-8884-5e74-8644-7b99e96a92b8" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281139 1034 "None" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281139 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534184 true] [17592186281139 1111 #uuid "ee1c10de-be68-546e-89d7-6c6bce31ea8e" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281140 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281140 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534184 true] [17592186281140 1111 #uuid "7c9e3412-b868-5fc7-b130-0f0ea9e47531" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281141 1034 "II only" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281141 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534184 true] [17592186281141 1111 #uuid "8e519c07-f571-5923-ad0e-ac376c5fb550" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281142 1017 #edb/ref 17592186281143 13194139534184 true] [17592186281142 1089 "q-48666" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281142 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534184 true] [17592186281142 1100 "Given that $f(x)={(5-3x)}^{4},$ find the equation of the tangent at point $(2,1).$" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281142 1113 #uuid "621014ba-46d4-530d-b830-042ea418b752" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281142 1145 "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\nFirst, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf={g}^{4},\\,g=5-3x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=4{g}^{3},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=-3.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =4{g}^{3}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-12(5-3x)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line at the point where $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & =-12{(5-3(2))}^{3} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the slope of the tangent line at the point $(2,1)$ is $m=12.$ Now, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =12(x-2) \\\\ y-1 & =12x-24 \\\\ y & =12x-23\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281143 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281144 13194139534184 true] [17592186281143 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281145 13194139534184 true] [17592186281143 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281146 13194139534184 true] [17592186281143 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281147 13194139534184 true] [17592186281143 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281148 13194139534184 true] [17592186281143 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534184 true] [17592186281143 1041 "selection" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281143 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281144 13194139534184 true] [17592186281143 1110 #uuid "57ecfdee-6185-5487-8e6c-57e620afee45" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281144 1034 "y=12x-23" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281144 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534184 true] [17592186281144 1111 #uuid "efa38dfd-ab13-532c-94ba-d17a224e8a8e" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281145 1034 "y=4x-7" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281145 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534184 true] [17592186281145 1111 #uuid "39bf0eac-7c48-5d70-b79b-881d89f635e3" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281146 1034 "y=-12x+25" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281146 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534184 true] [17592186281146 1111 #uuid "a07a9fc6-8f61-56c1-803e-40b619e646de" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281147 1034 "y=-3x+7" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281147 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534184 true] [17592186281147 1111 #uuid "7de81cd5-7fe1-516a-8402-9d92e9f9528b" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281148 1034 "y=-4x+9" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281148 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534184 true] [17592186281148 1111 #uuid "c746d33c-94c2-5309-8bfc-b21be2ee4d5a" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281149 1017 #edb/ref 17592186281150 13194139534184 true] [17592186281149 1089 "q-49234" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281149 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534184 true] [17592186281149 1100 "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that ${\\int }_{0}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[2{e}^{(k\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)/n}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{n}].$" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281149 1113 #uuid "6a62fd18-f127-592a-8fe3-1cc5a47bb7fb" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281149 1145 "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=0.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{n}=\\frac{b-0}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\n$$\n\nConsequently,  ${x}_{k}=\\frac{k\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{n}$ and $f({x}_{k})=2{e}^{{x}_{k}}.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}2{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[2{e}^{(k\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)/n}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(x)=2{e}^{x}$ and $b=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281150 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281151 13194139534184 true] [17592186281150 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281152 13194139534184 true] [17592186281150 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281153 13194139534184 true] [17592186281150 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281154 13194139534184 true] [17592186281150 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281155 13194139534184 true] [17592186281150 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534184 true] [17592186281150 1041 "selection" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281150 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281151 13194139534184 true] [17592186281150 1110 #uuid "d09793db-6d16-5b05-800e-e42e52935eec" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281151 1034 "$f(x)=2{e}^{x}$ and $b=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281151 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534184 true] [17592186281151 1111 #uuid "ff58b9c7-a5fc-54dd-b70e-3ac13c195484" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281152 1034 "$f(x)={e}^{2x}$ and $b=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281152 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534184 true] [17592186281152 1111 #uuid "f8fa9a38-512c-5c4c-957a-ef047727566b" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281153 1034 "$f(x)=2{e}^{x}$ and $b=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281153 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534184 true] [17592186281153 1111 #uuid "8dc3b0ba-87a0-5382-bb0f-1ff8949702b0" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281154 1034 "$f(x)={e}^{x}$ and $b=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281154 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534184 true] [17592186281154 1111 #uuid "c3b262c3-7043-5137-816b-2d7d8e664f27" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281155 1034 "$f(x)={e}^{x}$ and $b=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281155 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534184 true] [17592186281155 1111 #uuid "911aa7e1-f472-5ecf-b0e7-39fa5704683b" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281156 1017 #edb/ref 17592186281157 13194139534184 true] [17592186281156 1089 "q-80350" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281156 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534184 true] [17592186281156 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980518/assets/5e350d9b4db36831eac3ff0708a2acbc903c07265d4c6709632fb8a854121747.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the equation of the polynomial curve shown above?" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281156 1113 #uuid "57df23a6-895d-5827-9b2f-f73c89216f9f" 13194139534184 true] [17592186281156 1145 "First, we notice that the function has precisely three distinct roots, $x=-1$, $x=2$ and $x=5.$\n\nBased on the graph, we can make the following conclusions about the multiplicities of the roots:\n\n- Since the graph is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=-1,$ this root is also a simple root (the multiplicity equals $1$).\n\n- Since the graph passes through $x=2,$ this root has odd multiplicity, and since the graph is tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=2,$ the multiplicity must be greater than one.\n\n- Since the graph is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=5,$ this root is also a simple root (the multiplicity equals $1$).\n\nFrom the given options, the only possible equation is $y=(x+1)(x-2)^{5}(x-5).$" 13194139534184 true] [17592